drm_gfx: use the primary plane; sun4i overlays cannot scale

Two problems, both giving a black screen for every game while the RGUI menu
displayed correctly.

1. The plane-selection loop sets drm.use_primary as soon as it *encounters* a
   primary plane, never clears it, and does not break. Iterating planes
   33 (primary), 37, 41, 45 (overlays) ends with plane_id = 45 while
   use_primary is still true from plane 33.

   drm_surface_setup() runs BEFORE that loop and sizes the framebuffer from
   use_primary, so the buffer was allocated at core size (160x144 for Game Boy)
   and then handed to drmModeSetCrtc(), which cannot scale and requires the fb
   to cover the entire CRTC:

     [ERROR] [DRM]: failed to set CRTC for primary plane
     [INFO] [DRM]: primary/CRTC mode: src 160x144 -> 800x480

   The menu escaped this because toggling it re-runs setup with use_primary
   already true, allocating a full-screen buffer.

2. Preferring an overlay instead is not enough: the Allwinner display engine
   advertises overlay planes but rejects any SCALED drmModeSetPlane with
   EINVAL. Measured with modetest on a BPI-M2 Magic:

     -P 37@49:800x480@RG16       -> works
     -P 37@49:320x240*2.0@RG16   -> failed to enable plane: Invalid argument

   A libretro core almost never matches the panel mode, so the overlay path
   cannot carry game video here. drmModeSetPlane leaves the plane detached
   while reporting success - modetest shows "crtc 0, fb 0" for the plane
   RetroArch claims to be using.

So classify planes properly during the loop instead of clobbering the flag, and
select the primary plane, which takes a full-screen buffer scaled in software by
drm_surface_update() - the path the menu already used successfully. Revisit if a
platform turns up whose overlay planes do scale.

Also frees the drmModePlane on every path; the original leaked it on each
'continue'.

Tested on a BananaPi M2 Magic (A33) with a Waveshare 5inch DSI LCD (B) at
800x480, running gambatte (160x144).

Signed-off-by: RetroBPI_M2M

--- a/gfx/drivers/drm_gfx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers/drm_gfx.c
@@ -564,6 +564,13 @@
     *
     * Look at linux/source/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_plane_helper.c comments for more info.
     * Also, primary planes can't be scaled: we need overlays for that. */
+   /* The primary plane cannot be scaled and must cover the whole CRTC, so a
+    * core rendering smaller than the mode (160x144 Game Boy on an 800x480
+    * panel, say) can only be displayed through an OVERLAY. Track both and
+    * decide after the loop. */
+   uint32_t overlay_plane_id = 0;
+   uint32_t primary_plane_id = 0;
+
    for (i = 0; i < plane_resources->count_planes; i++)
    {
       plane = drmModeGetPlane(drm.fd, plane_resources->planes[i]);
@@ -574,29 +581,58 @@
          continue;
       }
 
-      /* Skip cursor planes; accept both overlay and primary */
+      /* Skip cursor planes. Classify the rest and pick after the loop. */
       {
          uint64_t ptype = drm_plane_type(plane);
+
          if (ptype == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR)
          {
             RARCH_LOG ("DRM: plane with ID %d is a cursor plane. Skipping.\n",
                   plane->plane_id);
+            drmModeFreePlane(plane);
             continue;
          }
-         if (ptype == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY)
-            drm.use_primary = true;
-      }
 
-      if (!format_support(plane, surface->pixformat))
-      {
-         RARCH_LOG ("DRM: plane with ID %d does not support framebuffer format\n", plane->plane_id);
-         continue;
+         if (!format_support(plane, surface->pixformat))
+         {
+            RARCH_LOG ("DRM: plane with ID %d does not support framebuffer format\n",
+                  plane->plane_id);
+            drmModeFreePlane(plane);
+            continue;
+         }
+
+         if (ptype == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY)
+         {
+            if (!overlay_plane_id)
+               overlay_plane_id = plane->plane_id;
+         }
+         else if (ptype == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY)
+         {
+            if (!primary_plane_id)
+               primary_plane_id = plane->plane_id;
+         }
       }
 
-      drm.plane_id = plane->plane_id;
       drmModeFreePlane(plane);
    }
 
+   /* Prefer the PRIMARY plane. The overlay cannot scale on this hardware
+    * (see drm_get_resources()), and drm_surface_setup() has already sized
+    * the framebuffer to match use_primary -- the two must agree or the
+    * buffer will not suit the path that consumes it. Fall back to an
+    * overlay only if there is no usable primary plane at all. */
+   if (primary_plane_id)
+   {
+      drm.plane_id    = primary_plane_id;
+      drm.use_primary = true;
+   }
+   else if (overlay_plane_id)
+   {
+      drm.plane_id    = overlay_plane_id;
+      drm.use_primary = false;
+      RARCH_LOG ("DRM: no primary plane, using overlay (scaling may fail)\n");
+   }
+
    if (!drm.plane_id)
    {
       RARCH_LOG ("DRM: couldn't find an usable overlay plane for current CRTC and framebuffer pixel formal.\n");
@@ -872,11 +908,21 @@
             }
          }
          drmModeFreePlaneResources(pr);
-         if (!has_overlay)
-         {
-            drm.use_primary = true;
-            RARCH_LOG("DRM: no overlay planes found, will use primary plane with CRTC mode\n");
-         }
+         /* The Allwinner display engine advertises overlay planes but
+          * rejects any SCALED drmModeSetPlane with EINVAL. Measured with
+          * modetest on a BPI-M2 Magic: an unscaled 800x480 overlay works,
+          * while a 320x240 source scaled 2x fails with
+          * "failed to enable plane: Invalid argument".
+          *
+          * A libretro core almost never matches the panel mode, so the
+          * overlay path cannot carry game video on this hardware. The
+          * primary plane takes a full-screen buffer and is scaled in
+          * software by drm_surface_update() -- the path the RGUI menu
+          * already used successfully. Revisit if a platform turns up
+          * whose overlay planes do scale. */
+         (void)has_overlay;
+         drm.use_primary = true;
+         RARCH_LOG("DRM: using primary plane with software scaling\n");
       }
    }
 
